    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="1021" n="911" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg911"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003/770: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-09-04T15:00:00+08:00">September 4, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 4—6:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>569. Department’s written instruction No. 550 of July 17.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>In comparing new draft with British draft we find that in article V the
                        words “or fine” after the words “for one year” (see British text telegraphed
                        April 19, 4 p.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d818-f1"/>) have been dropped. Will
                        Department <pb facs="1022" n="912" xml:id="pg912"/> inform me why these
                        words were dropped. They seemed to us necessary to make provisions
                        compatible with Chinese criminal code.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Why has Department dropped provision regarding court cases being heard in
                        Special Chambers from article VIII?</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>Why were words “of any” after the words “the option” in second paragraph
                        of article No. XIV dropped?</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
